# Survey to help building WEFE system

Right now it is a simple app to visualize the survey and test potential inputs for WEFE system builder

## Getting started

1. Create a virtual environment with python 3.10
2. Install the requirements with `pip install -r requirements.txt`
3. Apply the migration with `python manage.py migrate` (should only be runned once at initial setup)
4. Populate the database with survey questions `python manage.py update_survey_questions` (should only be runned once at initial setup)
5. Run the server `python manage.py runserver`

The survey is then accessible at http://127.0.0.1:8000/view/survey/<integer id of scenario> (you can input any integer during the test phase)
If you saved a survey visiting http://127.0.0.1:8000/view/survey/<integer id of scenario> will show you the answers, which you can then modify

If you edit the questions in survey/survey.py then you need to run `python manage.py update_survey_questions --update --dev` to edit within the app (if you create a new question, then the older saved surveys likely won't display it)

If you want to erase all questions of the survey from the database, then run `python manage.py purge_survey_questions`


Run the survey
fill it
export the survey results with python manage.py save_survey_answers <id of survey>, it saves it locally in the app folder in "scenario_<scen id>_survey_answers.json"
then move to the component_library/scripts/build_scenario.py file

There if you added a component to the library you need to rerun `python validate_component_lib.py` to recreate the datapackage.json file inside WIP_components folder (for this you need to clone oemof-tabular locally and checkout the branch `fix/datapackage`

Otherwise go at the end of `component_library/scripts/build_scenario.py` file and adapt the survey answer file after the `if __name__=="__main__":` statement